# .venv* (not .venv) — the voice worker installs into .venv-voice/, a SEPARATE
# Python 3.12 environment carrying livekit-agents and onnxruntime. It matched
# neither this pattern nor the root's, so a single `git add -A` would have
# committed roughly half a gigabyte of wheels.
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# env / secrets -- the same negated allowlist as the root .gitignore, repeated
# HERE deliberately. The root file already covers these names, so this block is
# not what makes them ignored today; it is what keeps them ignored the day
# somebody reorganises the root file, and it is the file a backend developer
# actually opens when they wonder whether `apps/api-py/.env` is safe. Two copies
# of a rule that must not silently disappear is cheaper than one copy that does.
#
# `apps/api-py/.env` is the file that carries AUTH_SECRET, VOICE_WORKER_SECRET,
# GROQ_API_KEY, the LIVEKIT_* triple and OPENAI_API_KEY -- and, per AGENTS.md,
# the SAME file the 3.12 voice worker reads, so it is the single densest
# credential file in the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets.json

# Local SQLite chat-memory bank
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# uploaded files (bytes on disk; only metadata is in the DB)
var/
